  "raw_text": "168\n\nMunpara\n \n(v\n-\nproh)\n \n–\n \ndo not do, do not try\n \n/ no lo hagas, no lo intentes\n\nMuns\n \n(\nv\n-\nimp\n)\n \n–\n \ndo\n \n/\n \nhaz, haga, hagan\n\nNahki munaia?\n \n–\n \nHow to do?\n;\n \nWhat to do?\n \n/ ¿Cómo hacer?; ¿Qué hacer?\n\nPadin munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto forgive\n \n/ perdonar\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nSwih tikaia\n)\n\nKupia wina padin munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto forgive from the heart\n \n/ perdonar desde el corazón\n\nPadin muni ba\n \n–\n \nforgiveness\n \n/ perdón\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nPadin lâka, Swih tikan lâka\n)\n\nPanis munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto punish, to chastise / castigar\n\nPaun munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto weigh\n \n/ pesar\n\nPint munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto paint, to draw\n \n/ pintar, dibujar\n\nPramis munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto promise\n \n/ prometer\n\nRau munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto hurt someone\n \n/ lastimar a alguien\n\nLatwan yabi rau munaia\n \n(\nbh46\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto torture\n \n/ torturar\n\nRau mamunra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nperson that hurts others\n \n/ persona que lastima a otros\n\nRau munan lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nviolence\n \n/ violencia\n\nRispik munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto respect\n \n/ respetar\n\nRug\n \n(a/t:\n \nRog\n \nand\n \nRuk\n)\n \nmunaia\n \n(Rug munaia)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto fornicate with someone, to commit immorality with someone, to\ncommit adultery with someone\n \n/ fornicar con alguien, cometer inmoralidad con alguien, cometer adulterio con\nalguien\n\nSaura munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto do harm to someone, to hurt someone, to do something bad to someone\n \n/ hacer daño a\nalguien, lastimar a alguien, hacer algo malo a alguien\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf-14\n):\n \nLalah briaia ba diara tara sa, sakuna maritkam lâka ra yarka saura munbiara bara uba trabil mai munbiara\n\n–\n \nIt is important to have money. However, you are not to allow it to harm your marriage nor to cause you anxiety.\n \n/ Es\nimportante tener dinero.\n \nSin embargo, no deb\ne\ns permitir\nle\n \ndañar\n \nt\nu matrimonio ni causar\nt\ne ansiedad.\n)\n\nPana saura munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto harm/hurt someone in return, to revenge\n \n/ dañar/lastimar a alguien\n \na cambio,\n\nvengarse\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nUpla kum saura wan munisa taim, pana saura munaia apia sa\n \n–\n \nWhen a person harms us, we are not to\n\nharm in return\n \n/ Cuando una persona nos perjudica, no debemos\n \nperjudicar\n \na cambio\n)\n\nSwer munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto swear to someone\n \n/ jurarle a alguien\n\nTaibi munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto step on someone, to tread on someone, to trample someone, to stamp on someone, to\n\npressure\n \nsomeone, to squeeze someone, to oppress someone, to defraud someone, to cheat someone, to\n\novercome someone, to force someone\n \n/ pisar a alguien, pisotear a alguien, presionar a alguien, apretar a\n\nalguien, oprimir a alguien, defraudar a alguien, engañar a alguien, vencer a alguien, forzar a alguien, obligar a\n\nalguien\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n09/20\n):\n \nNawas piua ra upla nani ba taibi wan munisa witin nani baku luki bara diara nani daukaia\n \n–\n \nIn\n\ntoday’s time, people pressure us to think and do things like them\n \n/ En la actualidad, la gente nos presiona para pensar y\n\nhacer cosas como ellos\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n05/21\n):\n \nJehova ai bila walbia taibi wan munras\n \n–\n \nJehovah does not force us to obey him\n \n/ Jehová no nos obliga\n\na obedecerle\n)\n\nTawa munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto handle with care, to be careful, to slow down, to be slow to get angry\n \n/ manejar con\ncuidado, tener cuidado, reducir la velocidad, ser lento para enojarse\n\nTrabil munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto trouble, to bother, to annoy, to cause distress, to cause anxiety\n \n/ molestar, causar ansiedad\n\nTrai munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto try, to attempt\n \n/ intentar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nll29\n):\n \nwitin baku kaia trai munaia sa\n \n–\n \nmust try to be like him\n \n/ debe tratar de ser como él)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n):\n \nNaha na trai muns\n \n–\n \nTry this\n \n/ Intente esto)\n\nKarna trai munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto try hard\n \n/ esforzarse\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-06/19\n):\n \nYawan karna trai munaia sa dîa daukaia luki ba Jehova kupia lâka kat kabia\n \n–\n \nWe must try\n\nhard to make the decision according to Jehovah’s\n \nwill\n \n/ Debemos esforzarnos por tomar la decisión de acuerdo\ncon la voluntad de Jehová)\n\nKarna trai muns\n \n(v-imp)\n \n–\n \ntry hard, endeavor\n \n/ esfuérzate\n\nTrai munaia ba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nthe attempt, the effort\n \n/ el intento, el esfuerzo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf25\n):\n \nMan dîa daukaia trai munisma ba Jehova yamni munbia\n \n–\n \nJehovah will reward your efforts\n \n/ Jehová\nrecompensará tus esfuerzos)\n\nTras munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto\n \ngive credit\n \n/\n \ndar crédito\n, fiar\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nTras ai muns pliskam\n \n–\n \nGive me credit please\n \n/ Me fia por favor\n)",
